00:34:39.150 --> 00:34:41.250
I mean, I knew he was going to throw trash cans at me.
我是说，我知道他要朝我扔垃圾桶。

973
00:34:41.570 --> 00:34:42.870
Oh, I was throwing trash cans at him.
哦，是我朝他扔垃圾桶。

974
00:34:42.870 --> 00:34:43.290
What am I saying?
我在说什么呢？

975
00:34:43.450 --> 00:34:46.490
But it was all like a weird, we had this whole negotiation and running thing.
但总之那就像是一种奇怪的互动，我们有一整套讨价还价和奔跑的桥段。

976
00:34:46.930 --> 00:34:51.730
And I was screaming so much, literally, when he was dragging me, once we got into the hospital,
而且当他拖着我的时候，我真的叫得太厉害了，一旦我们进了医院——

977
00:34:52.530 --> 00:34:55.450
Kelly Cantley was the attendant at the rehab center.
凯莉·坎特利饰演戒毒所的服务人员。

978
00:34:55.650 --> 00:34:56.210
Yes, that's right.
对，没错。

979
00:34:56.430 --> 00:34:58.070
Our assistant director played that.
我们的助理导演客串了那个角色。

980
00:34:58.210 --> 00:35:00.890
She had our first AD, and that was the only time I think she's ever been on an episode.
她担任过我们的第一副导演，而且我想那是她唯一一次在剧集中出镜。

981
00:35:01.190 --> 00:35:03.250
And I literally lost my voice by the end of that.
到那场戏结束时，我简直连嗓子都喊哑了。

982
00:35:03.330 --> 00:35:04.390
And it was totally worth it.
但这一切绝对都值了。

983
00:35:04.510 --> 00:35:05.350
It was totally worth it.
绝对值了。

984
00:35:05.490 --> 00:35:09.050
But that whole thing where I'm like negotiating, or Meredith saying like, wait a minute, wait
但还有我讨价还价的那整段，或者说梅雷迪思说的那种“等一下，等一下，

985
00:35:09.050 --> 00:35:09.790
a minute, wait a minute.
等一下”。

986
00:35:10.830 --> 00:35:11.150
Totally.
完全是这样。

987
00:35:11.350 --> 00:35:13.850
I was like, I was so happy that Paul Feig, he's like, do that again.
我当时就想，我特别高兴保罗·费格说：“再来一次。”

988
00:35:13.850 --> 00:35:16.330
He kept asking me to repeat certain things that I would say.
他一直让我重复我刚才说过的某些话。

989
00:35:16.470 --> 00:35:17.610
I'm like, oh, so yeah.
我就想，哦，好吧。

990
00:35:17.690 --> 00:35:20.370
I just saw Paul Feig last week at a women in film event.
我上周才在一次“影视女性”活动上见到保罗·费格。

991
00:35:20.370 --> 00:35:25.790
And we were just like, you know, just totally reminiscing about how wonderful it was to work
我们当时就在那里，你知道的，完全在深情回忆当初在《办公室》里

992
00:35:25.790 --> 00:35:26.630
together on The Office.
一起合作是多么美妙。

993
00:35:26.810 --> 00:35:27.250
Yeah.
对。

994
00:35:27.450 --> 00:35:28.190
So yeah.
所以，是的。

995
00:35:28.290 --> 00:35:31.810
Aren't you so thankful of all the directors it was Paul Feig?
你不觉得在所有的导演中偏偏是保罗·费格，真的很让人感恩吗？

996
00:35:31.930 --> 00:35:36.510
Because of course, Paul gave you all of that agency to just like, go for it.
因为当然了，保罗赋予了你们所有人那种完全可以放手去做的自主权。

997
00:35:36.650 --> 00:35:40.490
And then he supported you when you found a nugget that was really good.
而且当你发现一个真正精彩的灵感时，他会给予你支持。

998
00:35:40.770 --> 00:35:41.010
Totally.
完全同意。

999
00:35:41.470 --> 00:35:41.810
All right.
好了。

1000
00:35:41.810 --> 00:35:43.950
Are we ready for our final question?
我们准备好回答最后一个问题了吗？

1001
00:35:44.270 --> 00:35:44.550
Yeah.
是啊。

1002
00:35:44.830 --> 00:35:45.570
Here it is.
就是这个。

1003
00:35:46.190 --> 00:35:52.130
If you had to attend one Dunder Mifflin holiday party, which one would you pick?
如果你必须参加一个邓德米夫林的节日派对，你会选哪一个？

1004
00:35:52.490 --> 00:35:54.070
And now we're going to give you the choices.
现在我们要给出选项了。

1005
00:35:54.390 --> 00:35:55.190
We're going to give you the choices.
我们要给出选项了。

1006
00:35:55.390 --> 00:36:01.350
But basically, you're looking at a party either thrown by Angela, Pam, Phyllis, Jim and Dwight,
基本上，你要么去安吉拉、帕姆、菲利斯、吉姆和德怀特举办的派对，

1007
00:36:01.410 --> 00:36:01.970
or Andy.
要么去安迪的。

1008
00:36:02.430 --> 00:36:03.690
Jenna, why don't you list them off?
珍娜，你来念一下吧？

1009
00:36:03.770 --> 00:36:04.350
Here they are.
它们是这些。

1010
00:36:04.810 --> 00:36:07.710
Would you want to go to Christmas party?
你想去圣诞派对吗？

1011
00:36:08.170 --> 00:36:11.470
Angela's in charge of Christmas, and you're going to have a real sad Yankee swap.
安吉拉负责圣诞节，你会经历一场非常凄凉的白色大礼物交换。

1012
00:36:11.810 --> 00:36:14.110
Do you want to attend a Benihana Christmas?
你想去参加红花会圣诞节吗？

1013
00:36:14.530 --> 00:36:16.670
This is the dueling Christmas parties.
这是两个对立的圣诞派对。

1014
00:36:16.950 --> 00:36:19.490
You have Pam and Karen versus Angela.
帕姆和凯伦对阵安吉拉。

1015
00:36:20.330 --> 00:36:21.150
Moroccan Christmas.
摩洛哥圣诞节。

1016
00:36:21.150 --> 00:36:23.150
This is the one that Phyllis is in charge of.
这是菲利斯负责的那场。

1017
00:36:23.290 --> 00:36:24.950
This ends in Meredith's intervention.
这场以干预梅雷迪思告终。

1018
00:36:25.550 --> 00:36:26.270
And burnt hair.
还有烧焦的头发。

1019
00:36:26.450 --> 00:36:26.930
And yes.
没错。

1020
00:36:27.010 --> 00:36:27.770
Hair on fire.
头发着火了。

1021
00:36:27.930 --> 00:36:28.090
Yes.
是的。

1022
00:36:28.250 --> 00:36:29.070
While she's belly dancing.
当她在跳肚皮舞的时候。

1023
00:36:29.270 --> 00:36:29.570
Thank you.
谢谢。

1024
00:36:30.890 --> 00:36:33.050
There's also Secret Santa.
还有神秘圣诞老人。

1025
00:36:33.430 --> 00:36:35.270
This was Jim and Dwight's holiday party.
这是吉姆和德怀特的节日派对。

1026
00:36:35.490 --> 00:36:36.850
We had dueling Santas.
我们有两个圣诞老人。

1027
00:36:37.010 --> 00:36:40.390
You had both Phyllis and Michael as Santa and Michael as Jesus.
菲利斯和迈克尔都是圣诞老人，迈克尔还是耶稣。

1028
00:36:40.510 --> 00:36:44.990
I was sitting on Phyllis's lap when Kevin was sitting on Michael Scott's lap at the same
我坐在菲利斯的腿上，同时凯文坐在迈克尔·斯科特的腿上，

1029
00:36:44.990 --> 00:36:45.290
time.
就在同一时间。

1030
00:36:45.490 --> 00:36:47.230
Oh, that's so great.
哦，那太棒了。

1031
00:36:47.910 --> 00:36:48.930
Try not to laugh.
尽量别笑。

1032
00:36:49.250 --> 00:36:51.150
You could attend a classy Christmas.
你可以参加一个高档的圣诞节。

1033
00:36:51.150 --> 00:36:56.490
This is when Pam was in charge of a regular Christmas that got turned into a bigger, fancier
这是帕姆负责普通圣诞节的时候，结果变成了一个更大、更豪华的

1034
00:36:56.490 --> 00:36:57.970
party to impress Holly.
派对，为了给霍莉留下好印象。

1035
00:36:58.670 --> 00:37:03.730
Michael has kind of a meltdown, and there's the insane snowball fight with Jim and Dwight.
迈克尔有点情绪崩溃，还有吉姆和德怀特疯狂的雪球大战。

1036
00:37:04.070 --> 00:37:05.350
There's Christmas wishes.
还有圣诞愿望。

1037
00:37:05.850 --> 00:37:07.070
Andy's in charge of Christmas.
安迪负责圣诞节。

1038
00:37:07.770 --> 00:37:09.410
Dwight and Jim prank each other.
德怀特和吉姆互相恶作剧。

1039
00:37:09.710 --> 00:37:11.790
Robert California announces his divorce.
罗伯特·加利福尼亚宣布离婚。

1040
00:37:12.190 --> 00:37:13.430
That's always fun at a party.
在派对上这总是很有趣。

1041
00:37:13.430 --> 00:37:20.110
Or, finally, Dwight's Christmas, he throws the traditional shrewd holiday party with bell
或者最后，德怀特的圣诞节，他举办了传统的精明节日派对，有黑面

1042
00:37:20.110 --> 00:37:23.210
schnickel, and you are either impish or admirable.
泥巴，你是淘气还是乖巧。

1043
00:37:23.350 --> 00:37:25.870
And you get swatted at with a bunch of sticks.
然后你会被一捆棍子抽打。

1044
00:37:26.290 --> 00:37:28.910
Which Christmas party would you like to attend?
你想参加哪个圣诞派对？

1045
00:37:29.110 --> 00:37:31.990
Well, this is like picking your favorite child.
好吧，这就像是在选你最喜欢的孩子。

1046
00:37:32.330 --> 00:37:33.930
You really cannot do it.
你真的做不到。

1047
00:37:34.030 --> 00:37:34.390
Can you?
对吧？

1048
00:37:34.790 --> 00:37:36.230
It's really juSt...
这真的是……

1049
00:37:36.230 --> 00:37:36.650
I don't know.
我不知道。

1050
00:37:36.710 --> 00:37:39.190
Some of these children are much worse than the others.
有些孩子比其他的差远了。

1051
00:37:40.390 --> 00:37:46.150
But I will actually say, I had the most fun shooting Rockin' Christmas, but I will say
不过我真的得说，拍《摇滚圣诞》的时候我最开心，但我得说

1052
00:37:46.150 --> 00:37:49.450
A Christmas Party, the first one, was my favorite.
第一集《圣诞派对》是我的最爱。

1053
00:37:49.610 --> 00:37:54.930
Because we were in new territory for the show, for Diner Mifflin.
因为那是我们节目、对于迪纳·米夫林来说的新领域。

1054
00:37:55.050 --> 00:37:59.950
It was just, you know, remember, do you guys remember the big tree that didn't fit?
那就是，你知道的，记得吗，你们还记得那棵放不进的大树吗？

1055
00:38:00.130 --> 00:38:00.690
Yes.
记得。

1056
00:38:00.690 --> 00:38:01.910
They had to get the biggest tree.
他们非得弄最大的一棵树。

1057
00:38:01.930 --> 00:38:02.110
Yes, amazing.
对，太棒了。

1058
00:38:02.510 --> 00:38:05.750
And then Yankee Swap, which was endless but fantastic.
还有白色象牙交换礼物，虽然没完没了但棒极了。

1059
00:38:06.290 --> 00:38:07.390
That group scene.
那个群戏场面。

1060
00:38:07.390 --> 00:38:10.470
It was like the weight of a brick.
就像砖头一样重。

1061
00:38:10.750 --> 00:38:12.470
Like, that's how old this episode is.
就像，这集都这么老了。

1062
00:38:12.570 --> 00:38:12.990
I know.
我知道。

1063
00:38:13.150 --> 00:38:13.790
The old tech.
老式科技。

1064
00:38:14.210 --> 00:38:15.370
I'm with you, Kate.
我支持你，凯特。

1065
00:38:15.530 --> 00:38:22.870
I'm with you because I felt like that group scene of us all in a circle handing out the
我支持你，因为我觉得我们大家围成一圈派发礼物的那个群戏

1066
00:38:22.870 --> 00:38:27.010
gifts is one of my favorite group scenes we ever did on the show.
是我在剧中最喜欢的群戏之一。

1067
00:38:27.570 --> 00:38:30.490
Everyone had a moment, and it was just amazing.
每个人都有高光时刻，真是太棒了。

1068
00:38:31.010 --> 00:38:32.570
I'm going to go another way, guys.
我选别的，伙计们。

1069
00:38:32.690 --> 00:38:33.230
Where are you going?
你选哪个？

1070
00:38:33.530 --> 00:38:37.110
I'm going with a Benihana Christmas, the dueling Christmas parties.
我选《贝尼哈纳圣诞节》，两场针锋相对的圣诞派对。

1071
00:38:38.510 --> 00:38:45.650
I just loved, because we had the singing and everything, and I loved that in the conference
我就是喜欢，因为我们有歌唱什么的，我喜欢会议室里的

1072
00:38:45.650 --> 00:38:46.170
room.
那个场景。

1073
00:38:46.390 --> 00:38:47.550
Pam and Karen had booze.
帕姆和凯伦有酒。

1074
00:38:47.610 --> 00:38:49.370
It was, yeah, it was like two parties.
真的，就像有两个派对一样。

1075
00:38:49.370 --> 00:38:50.830
You can go to two parties.
你可以去两个派对。

1076
00:38:51.010 --> 00:38:52.830
But Angela had, I think, some good food.
但安吉拉有，我觉得，一些好吃的。

1077
00:38:53.130 --> 00:38:56.210
You had some good, like, treats and cookies and things.
你们有一些不错的，比如点心、饼干之类的好东西。

1078
00:38:56.330 --> 00:38:56.530
Yeah.
对。

1079
00:38:56.530 --> 00:38:57.550
So, I don't know.
所以，我不知道。

1080
00:38:57.670 --> 00:39:02.450
If I had to attend a party just as a guest, I think I might like to show up at the dueling
如果我只是作为客人去参加派对，我想我可能会想去那场针锋相对的

1081
00:39:02.450 --> 00:39:03.170
Christmas parties.
圣诞派对。

1082
00:39:03.290 --> 00:39:10.910
If I had to go back in time and re-experience shooting a Christmas episode, then I think,
如果我必须回到过去，重新体验拍摄圣诞单集，那么我觉得，

1083
00:39:12.470 --> 00:39:14.470
gosh, that's very difficult.
天哪，这太难了。

1084
00:39:14.730 --> 00:39:16.830
But then I'd have to go to the original Christmas party.
但那我还是得去最初的那场圣诞派对。

1085
00:39:16.830 --> 00:39:17.610
Okay, so same.
好吧，我也是。

1086
00:39:17.770 --> 00:39:26.430
So, if me, Angela, me, Kinsey, Martin, wanted to revisit, it would be Yankee Swap, because
所以，如果我，安吉拉，我，金西，马丁，想要重温，那就是白色象牙交换礼物，因为

1087
00:39:26.430 --> 00:39:29.810
I just want to live in that group scene again, just selfishly.
我只是想自私地再次重温那个群戏。

1088
00:39:29.810 --> 00:39:37.450
But if I'm just a party-goer, I think I would pick Secret Santa, because I love the idea
但如果我只是个派对动物，我想我会选择秘密圣诞老人，因为我喜欢

1089
00:39:37.450 --> 00:39:40.270
of two Santas and Jesus all at the same party.
两个圣诞老人和一个耶稣同时出现在一个派对上的想法。

1090
00:39:40.410 --> 00:39:40.970
Yeah, that's pretty great.
对，那真是太棒了。

1091
00:39:40.970 --> 00:39:42.130
That's how I pick a great party.
这就是我挑选好派对的标准。

1092
00:39:42.130 --> 00:39:43.110
That was my runner-up.
那是我的第二选择。

1093
00:39:43.270 --> 00:39:43.410
Right.
没错。

1094
00:39:43.450 --> 00:39:43.630
Yeah.
对。

1095
00:39:43.890 --> 00:39:50.190
Well, I'm still like, I think Meredith is all in for the first Christmas episode, and so
好吧，我还是觉得，梅雷迪思完全支持第一集圣诞特辑，

1096
00:39:50.190 --> 00:39:50.450
is Kate.
凯特也是。

1097
00:39:50.650 --> 00:39:54.310
Well, Kate, thank you so much for being on our holiday chit-chat episode.
好吧，凯特，非常感谢你来参加我们的节日闲聊节目。

1098
00:39:54.550 --> 00:39:56.930
The folks at Macy sent a gift card for you.
梅西百货的人给你寄了一张礼品卡。

1099
00:39:57.130 --> 00:39:58.230
They sure did.
确实寄了。

1100
00:39:58.230 --> 00:39:59.410
Here you go, Kate.
给你，凯特。

1101
00:39:59.410 --> 00:40:02.330
Kate, happy shopping from the folks at Macy's.
凯特，来自梅西百货的朋友们祝你购物愉快。

1102
00:40:02.390 --> 00:40:03.870
Thank you so much, Macy's.
非常感谢，梅西百货。

1103
00:40:03.970 --> 00:40:05.050
I didn't get you anything.
我什么都没送你们。

1104
00:40:05.050 --> 00:40:06.070
I'm so sorry.
真是太不好意思了。

1105
00:40:06.210 --> 00:40:08.650
I feel really, I didn't buy Macy's anything.
我真的觉得，我没给梅西百货买任何东西。

1106
00:40:10.010 --> 00:40:11.310
So sorry, you guys.
非常抱歉，伙计们。

1107
00:40:12.450 --> 00:40:14.530
Oh, Kate, this is so fun.
哦，凯特，这太有意思了。

1108
00:40:14.910 --> 00:40:15.590
So fun.
太有意思了。

1109
00:40:15.770 --> 00:40:19.790
I mean, Kate, I do kind of feel like I need you to lead us in a Christmas carol.
我是说，凯特，我确实觉得我需要你带头唱一首圣诞颂歌。

1110
00:40:20.650 --> 00:40:21.010
Yes.
好呀。

1111
00:40:21.550 --> 00:40:22.410
Are they free?
那些是免费的吗？

1112
00:40:22.690 --> 00:40:23.530
Can we have one?
我们可以来一首吗？

1113
00:40:23.690 --> 00:40:25.190
I know a bunch that are free.
我知道很多免费的。

1114
00:40:25.330 --> 00:40:25.710
You know some?
你知道一些？

1115
00:40:25.710 --> 00:40:28.890
I'm trying to think of, like, something from the office, and the only thing I can think of
我在努力想那种，办公室的歌，我能想到的唯一一首

1116
00:40:28.890 --> 00:40:33.290
is, come, they told me by rump, rump, rump, rump, rump.
就是，来吧，他们告诉我伴着咚，咚，咚，咚，咚。

1117
00:40:33.570 --> 00:40:34.370
Da-da-da-da.
哒哒哒哒。

1118
00:40:34.630 --> 00:40:35.070
Da-da-da-da.
哒哒哒哒。

1119
00:40:38.390 --> 00:40:40.210
That was still an Angela's song.
那依然是安吉拉的歌。

1120
00:40:40.370 --> 00:40:41.270
Thank you, guys.
谢谢你们，伙计们。

1121
00:40:41.530 --> 00:40:44.490
And thank you to the folks at Macy's for supporting Office Ladies.
还要感谢梅西百货的朋友们对《办公室女士》的支持。

1122
00:40:44.710 --> 00:40:46.430
We love these holiday bonus episodes.
我们超爱这些节日特别番外集。

1123
00:40:46.690 --> 00:40:47.470
We love you guys.
我们爱你们。

1124
00:40:47.650 --> 00:40:48.930
Kate, thanks for coming in.
凯特，谢谢你来作客。

1125
00:40:49.130 --> 00:40:50.350
Thank you so much, you guys.
